Edition No. 30 — Friday, 30 October 2026

10 stories: 'This is the last adjournment': Mundubile, Zulu and 16 others appear at last, and the High Court sets 5 November for the bail hearing as the State asks for time to read the reply (lead); One name left on the Mandevu ballot: all three of Adrian Banda's rivals withdraw a week before polling day, and the FDD's Daniel Chisenga says threats to his family forced him out; The last two desks filled: Milupi takes Transport and Logistics, Kalila takes Housing with an order that councils allocate only serviced land, and Mulusa returns as Chief Whip; Inflation edges up to 6.3 per cent as diesel jumps 24 per cent in a month, and September's trade balance swings to a US$186 million deficit on weaker copper exports; US$31 billion to 2050 and a US$23.1 billion hole for ZESCO: the Energy Ministry's financing strategy for the power plan, as the Permanent Secretary puts capacity at 4,722 MW; 1,622 cases and 30 deaths, more than half of them before reaching a clinic: Chilengi tells Parliament the outbreak has spread to 20 districts as 709,018 people are vaccinated; Mapatizya falls vacant: the High Court at Livingstone nullifies Emeldah Munashabantu's election over the ECZ's handling of the count, finds the MP blameless and awards costs; A final in Baku: Zambia's under-15s beat Slovakia 3–1 and Senegal 4–3 in one day and meet Portugal for the Tier B title on Friday, with Maxen Msimuko on 13 goals; Maniema Union, Singida Black Stars and a club still to be decided: Red Arrows learn their Confederation Cup group, with the first matches from 27 November; Six for Senegal: a judoka, a badminton player, three swimmers and a sprinter carry Zambia into the first Olympic event held in Africa, which opens in Dakar on Saturday.

